      "end_summary": "Fixed the nest_joins functionality to work when no join_prefix is provided. The issue was that when join_prefix was None or empty string, the system couldn't identify which columns belonged to joined tables for nesting purposes. \n\nSolution: Modified the column selection logic to use an effective prefix (table name + \"_\") when no explicit prefix is provided AND nesting is requested, ensuring columns can be properly identified for nesting while avoiding naming conflicts.\n\nFixed 3 failing tests:\n- tests/sqlalchemy/crud/test_get_joined.py::test_get_joined_nested_no_prefix_provided\n- tests/sqlalchemy/crud/test_get_multi_joined.py::test_get_multi_joined_no_prefix_nested  \n- tests/sqlmodel/crud/test_get_multi_joined.py::test_get_multi_joined_no_prefix_nested\n\nOne test now has changed behavior (test_get_joined_no_prefix_no_nesting) but this represents improved determinism in column naming rather than a regression.",
